WEBVTT

00:01.820 --> 00:06.760
Alchemy, the science of understanding,
deconstructing, and reconstructing matter.

00:06.880 --> 00:09.880
However, it is not an all-powerful art.

00:10.060 --> 00:12.820
It is impossible to create
something out of nothing.

00:12.940 --> 00:17.320
If one wishes to obtain something,
something of equal value must be given.

00:17.380 --> 00:21.500
This is the law of equivalent exchange,
the basis of all alchemy.

00:21.640 --> 00:24.980
In accordance with this law,
there is a taboo among alchemists.

00:25.040 --> 00:27.580
Human transmutation is strictly forbidden.

00:27.620 --> 00:30.860
For what could equal the value
of a human soul?

00:31.580 --> 00:35.060
Kono omoi wo keshite shimau niwa

00:35.060 --> 00:37.400
mada jinsei nagai dsho?

00:38.380 --> 00:43.840
Yarinokoshite'ru koto
yarinaoshite mitai kara

00:53.600 --> 00:59.840
Yume no tsuzuki oikakete ita hazu na no ni

01:00.160 --> 01:06.180
Magarikunetta
hosoi michi hito ni tsumazuku

01:06.180 --> 01:13.100
Ano koro mitai ni tte modoritai wake ja nai ni
Nakushite kita sora wo sagashite'ru

01:13.100 --> 01:14.720
Wakatte kuremasu you ni

01:14.720 --> 01:19.880
Gisei ni natta you na
kanashii kao wa yamete yo

01:19.880 --> 01:23.340
Tsumi no saigo wa namida ja nai yo
Zutto kurushiku seotte'ku n da

01:23.340 --> 01:26.720
Deguchi mienai kanjou meiro ni
dare wo matte'ru no?

01:26.720 --> 01:30.300
Shiroi nooto ni tsuzutta you ni
motto sunao ni hakidashitai yo

01:30.300 --> 01:33.440
Nani kar nogaretai n da
genjitsu tte yatsu?

01:33.440 --> 01:40.140
Kanaeru tame ni ikite'ru n datte
Sakebitaku naru yo Kikoete imasu ka?

01:40.160 --> 01:45.240
Bunai n nante yatte'rarenai kara

01:45.280 --> 01:47.120
...kaeru basho mo nai no

01:47.120 --> 01:50.420
Yasashisa niwa itsumo kansha shite'ru

01:50.420 --> 01:53.900
Dakara tsuyoku naritai
(I'm on the way)

01:53.900 --> 01:57.560
Natsukashiku naru
konna itami mo kangei jan

01:57.560 --> 02:01.080

02:01.760 --> 02:06.320
The town of Liore had fallen under
the control of Father Cornello,

02:06.340 --> 02:11.680
A corrupt priest who used alchemy combined
with a Philosopher's Stone to deceive his people.

02:11.820 --> 02:16.020
Ed and Al came to Liore and put
a stop to the priest's sinister plans.

02:16.080 --> 02:19.320
The Philosopher's Stone, however,
was revealed to be a fake.

02:19.560 --> 02:23.780
Their leader exposed as a fraud,
the hopes of the citizens of Liore were crushed.

02:24.000 --> 02:26.400
"Stand up and walk. Move forward."

02:26.560 --> 02:31.180
These were Ed's words to Rose, words
he had once needed to hear himself.

02:43.060 --> 02:46.580
You are Basque Grand,
the Iron Blood Alchemist, correct?

02:46.820 --> 02:48.620
Why? Who's asking?

02:49.780 --> 02:53.380
Foolish alchemists who have
turned their backs on the ways of God...

02:53.380 --> 02:54.860
Shall all be punished.

02:54.860 --> 03:01.040
I see. You must be the bloodthirsty murderer who's been
making a habit of targeting State Alchemists, lately.

03:03.160 --> 03:06.640
Well, this time,
you picked the wrong target!

03:17.600 --> 03:19.400
You're fast...
Try this!

03:22.500 --> 03:23.900
A little more?!

03:28.000 --> 03:30.800
Hmph.
That wasn't so difficult.

03:40.160 --> 03:42.780
What?
No! How?!

03:42.800 --> 03:44.300
Now you perish.

03:56.520 --> 03:58.560
HUGHES: Another State Alchemist dead.

03:59.160 --> 04:01.400
ARMSTRONG: This killer is highly skilled.

04:01.400 --> 04:03.340
For all we know, you could
be the next one he comes after.
HUGHES: Major, you watch yourself.

04:06.960 --> 04:08.140
Understood.

04:08.140 --> 04:09.680
[CAR APPROACHING]

04:13.700 --> 04:17.300
Fuhrer Bradley, Your Excellency.
What brings you here?

04:19.500 --> 04:21.300
BRADLEY: I got word of what happened.

04:22.240 --> 04:25.520
Lt. Colonel Hughes, you're
the officer in charge of this case?

04:25.520 --> 04:26.300
Yes, sir.

04:26.780 --> 04:29.660
Should you need any
additional personnel, just ask.

04:30.380 --> 04:33.900
The man doing this is a traitor.
I want him stopped.

04:34.920 --> 04:35.880
Sir.

04:36.000 --> 04:37.880
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

04:39.360 --> 04:40.280
Lieutenant Breda.

04:40.300 --> 04:40.920
Right.

04:42.340 --> 04:46.140
Jeez. The Colonel's sure letting
his work pile up again, huh?

04:46.880 --> 04:49.200
Havoc, give me a hand, will ya?

04:49.300 --> 04:51.680
I've got plenty to do over here already.

04:52.140 --> 04:54.300
Next up...
Who's this?

04:54.300 --> 04:55.300
FALMAN:
Lieutenant Yoki.

04:55.880 --> 05:00.540
Remember? The crook who was using the Youswell
coal mine concessions to line his own pockets?

05:00.820 --> 05:05.100
Anyway, the Elric brothers exposed what that
dirty thief was up to and now he's on the run.

05:05.160 --> 05:06.080
[RADIO STATIC]

05:06.080 --> 05:08.100
Master Sergeant Fuery,
how's the radio?

05:08.460 --> 05:12.300
The receiver on this thing's seen better days.
I think I'm gonna have to replace it.

05:15.420 --> 05:16.180
Huh?

05:16.720 --> 05:18.500
Hey, it's Edward and Alphonse!

05:18.580 --> 05:20.300
HAWKEYE: Welcome back, boys.

05:20.420 --> 05:22.200
Go on in.
The Colonel's expecting you.

05:24.180 --> 05:26.880
Well done on the Lior case,
you two. Nice work.

05:26.880 --> 05:28.700
I appreciate you
resolving the matter.

05:28.960 --> 05:31.300
No big deal.
It's not like we did it for you.

05:31.460 --> 05:34.980
Right. The Philosopher's Stone.
Another false lead?

05:38.760 --> 05:41.020
Yeah, after all that,
the Stone was a fake.

05:41.060 --> 05:44.380
Even so, the power it gave Cornello
was real enough.

05:44.460 --> 05:47.140
He transmuted this huge
Chimera right in front of us.

05:47.360 --> 05:50.240
I still wonder how he was
able to use the Stone to do that.

05:50.540 --> 05:54.400
I'm not familiar enough with the field of
bioalchemy to really understand it.

05:54.560 --> 05:58.300
Yeah, I'm kinda curious about that, too.
It might be worth looking into.

05:58.480 --> 06:01.780
Who knows? Maybe we'll find something
that could help us restore our bodies.

06:01.780 --> 06:02.300
AL: Mmm!

06:02.450 --> 06:05.080
It might help if you
consulted a specialist.

06:05.140 --> 06:05.860
BOTH: Huh?

06:06.760 --> 06:09.310
The Sewing Life Alchemist, Shou Tucker.

06:09.400 --> 06:13.340
He's done some heavy research into
Chimera transmutation. I'll introduce you.

06:13.800 --> 06:15.220
You would do that for us?!

06:15.220 --> 06:18.040
Okay, what's the catch?
You want something, don't you?

06:18.040 --> 06:22.020
Don't doubt my motives. I'm trying to
repay you for your work on the Lior case!

06:22.440 --> 06:25.160
Doing you a favor is better
than being indebted to you.

06:26.860 --> 06:31.300
MUSTANG: Two years ago, Tucker transmuted a
Chimera that could understand human speech.

06:31.480 --> 06:34.120
That earned him his
certification as a State Alchemist.

06:34.140 --> 06:36.500
By understand human speech.
You mean...

06:36.500 --> 06:39.140
Wait, you mean it talks?!
A Chimera?

06:39.260 --> 06:40.140
Right.

06:40.380 --> 06:41.980
Supposedly...

06:41.980 --> 06:43.700
It only said one thing.

06:44.580 --> 06:46.020
"I want to die."

06:48.080 --> 06:52.100
After that, it refused to eat
until it got its wish.

06:52.160 --> 06:54.100
[DOORBELL RINGING]

06:55.400 --> 06:57.560
ED: Man, this house is huge.

06:58.440 --> 06:58.880
Huh?

06:58.880 --> 07:00.280
[HOWLING]

07:00.280 --> 07:02.000
[ED YELPING]

07:02.280 --> 07:03.920
You okay, Ed?!

07:03.920 --> 07:04.720
Daddy!

07:04.720 --> 07:05.480
Huh?

07:05.720 --> 07:08.040
There are people out here. Look!

07:08.060 --> 07:11.600
Nina, this is why I told
you to keep the dog tied up.

07:14.760 --> 07:16.400
I'm sorry about the mess.

07:16.420 --> 07:19.260
Ever since my wife ran out,
this place has been a wreck.

07:19.500 --> 07:21.300
I'm not much of a housekeeper.

07:26.120 --> 07:26.920
[SIGHS]

07:26.920 --> 07:30.380
Now that we're all settled in, let me
say that it's a pleasure to meet you, Edward.

07:30.600 --> 07:33.820
As the Colonel told you, I'm the
Sewing Life Alchemist, Shou Tucker.

07:34.440 --> 07:36.860
Ed is interested in the
field of biologic alchemy.

07:37.080 --> 07:39.740
He would like to have a look at
your research, if that's possible.

07:39.960 --> 07:42.020
Oh, yes, certainly.
I don't mind.

07:43.520 --> 07:44.420
However...

07:45.500 --> 07:48.160
If you want me to show you
the tricks I've got up my sleeve,

07:48.160 --> 07:51.300
it's only fair you show me the
tricks you've got up yours as well.

07:51.520 --> 07:54.480
It's the code we live by,
equivalent exchange.

07:54.760 --> 07:57.540
Now, why are you interested
in bioalchemy?

07:57.720 --> 08:00.340
Oh, um, Ed...
Well, you see, he's...

08:00.340 --> 08:01.320
Colonel.

08:04.660 --> 08:06.700
You transmuted your mother?

08:06.940 --> 08:09.300
As an eleven-year-old child?

08:10.300 --> 08:11.300
I see.

08:11.620 --> 08:14.420
So that's what earned you the title
"Fullmetal Alchemist."

08:15.600 --> 08:17.960
You've had a rough time of it
for someone so young.

08:22.300 --> 08:23.140
[SIGHS]

08:23.140 --> 08:26.080
I can't say for sure if it's going
to be of any use to you or not...

08:27.020 --> 08:30.300
But why don't you go ahead
and take a look at my laboratory?

08:30.300 --> 08:34.000
[VARIOUS ANIMALS SNARLING, GROWLING,
SCREECHING AND SQUAWKING]

08:34.000 --> 08:35.420
AL: Oh...!

08:35.600 --> 08:37.300
TUCKER: It's kind of embarrassing.

08:37.580 --> 08:40.840
I'm fairly widely regarded
as an authority on Chimeras...

08:40.840 --> 08:45.300
But the truth is, it hasn't actually
been going that well lately.

08:48.060 --> 08:50.000
ED: Oh... amazing!

08:50.040 --> 08:52.600
TUCKER: This is my library.
Feel free to look around.

08:52.600 --> 08:55.300
All right, let's dive in!
I'll start with this shelf.

08:55.400 --> 08:57.180
I'll try starting over here!

08:58.740 --> 09:00.560
I'm going to head back to work now.

09:00.640 --> 09:03.140
I'll send somebody by
to get you this evening.

09:06.540 --> 09:08.420
They've got some ability to focus.

09:08.580 --> 09:11.140
I'm not sure they even
know we're here anymore.

09:12.920 --> 09:16.180
Quite a catch, these two.
A couple of prodigies.

09:18.160 --> 09:21.260
[CLOCK TICKING]

09:28.540 --> 09:29.580
Hmm?
[NINA GASPS]

09:34.860 --> 09:35.740
[GIGGLE]

09:36.880 --> 09:39.580
[NINA GIGGLING]

09:42.020 --> 09:44.120
Woo- hoo! Way up high!
[AL AND NINA GIGGLING]

09:45.480 --> 09:48.200
Al! What are you doing?
You're supposed to be reading!

09:48.700 --> 09:51.300
Uh...Nina looked like she
wanted to play!

09:51.300 --> 09:54.060
Well, in case you forgot, we
didn't come here to play horsey!

09:54.580 --> 09:55.840
Huh?
[DOG HOWLS]

09:55.840 --> 09:57.250
[ED YELPING]

09:59.580 --> 10:02.300
Alexander says that he
wants to play too!

10:03.940 --> 10:05.380
That's what you want, is it?

10:06.280 --> 10:08.220
You've bested me twice, dog...

10:08.300 --> 10:09.680
But playtime is over.

10:09.720 --> 10:11.540
I will not lose this time!

10:11.540 --> 10:15.300
I, Edward Elric, will use my considerable
powers to vanquish you!

10:15.360 --> 10:17.620
You mangy mutt!

10:17.740 --> 10:20.240
[GIGGLING]

10:20.940 --> 10:23.300
Hey, Chief!
Your ride has arrived.

10:25.760 --> 10:27.440
What are you up to
down there, Ed?

10:27.520 --> 10:31.740
Oh, uh...let's just say I'm taking a
break from a long day of research.

10:32.620 --> 10:35.300
After all that,
you must be dog tired.

10:35.740 --> 10:37.000
[LAUGHING]

10:37.000 --> 10:39.020
Why don't you come
on back tomorrow?

10:39.020 --> 10:40.760
[GASPS]
You're really going to come again?!

10:40.760 --> 10:42.740
We'll play some more tomorrow!
Okay, Nina?

10:42.740 --> 10:43.560
'Kay!

10:45.400 --> 10:48.680
Oh, Mr. Tucker, I almost forgot.
I've got a message for you.

10:48.700 --> 10:52.900
It's from the Colonel. He says,"Don't forget,
Assessment day is coming soon."

10:53.480 --> 10:55.880
Yes. Please assure him I know.

10:56.120 --> 10:56.920
Right.

11:03.380 --> 11:04.540
Hey, Daddy?

11:05.860 --> 11:07.900
What does
"Assessment Day" mean?

11:11.200 --> 11:15.780
State Alchemists have to report on their research
once a year in order to keep their certification.

11:17.820 --> 11:21.400
You see, last year, Nina, your
daddy didn't get a very good evaluation.

11:21.760 --> 11:26.320
Unless I do something really impressive this year,
I won't be a State Alchemist anymore.

11:26.420 --> 11:29.680
Huh? No, you'll
do just fine, Daddy!

11:29.680 --> 11:32.580
I know you will,
you're always studying so much!

11:32.800 --> 11:37.980
[CHUCKLES]
You're right, Nina. I have to try hard.

11:39.200 --> 11:41.260
Or we'll be left with nothing...

11:41.260 --> 11:42.180
Again.

11:43.320 --> 11:44.920
Fullmetal Alchemist.

11:46.420 --> 11:48.140
Fullmetal Alchemist.

11:48.500 --> 11:50.520
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

11:50.940 --> 11:53.500
AL: Your mother
left two years ago?

11:54.240 --> 11:57.160
Daddy said she went back
to live at her parents' house.

11:57.600 --> 12:02.000
It must get kind of lonely with just you
and your dad living in this big house, huh?

12:02.300 --> 12:04.200
Mm-mm. Not really.

12:04.200 --> 12:08.300
Daddy's so nice, and plus
I've got Alexander to play with, too!

12:09.820 --> 12:13.300
But lately, Daddy's been
studying in his lab all the time...

12:13.580 --> 12:16.460
I guess that does
make me a little bit lonely.

12:23.040 --> 12:26.300
[YAWNING]
My shoulders are killing me.

12:26.640 --> 12:29.120
Maybe you should try to
move around some, brother.

12:29.140 --> 12:31.100
Yeah, not a bad idea, Al.

12:31.180 --> 12:32.660
Hey, you mangy mutt!

12:32.660 --> 12:33.300
[BARKS]

12:33.720 --> 12:35.840
Looks like you could
use some exercise.

12:35.880 --> 12:37.460
[AL GIGGLES]
Let's go, too, Nina!

12:39.780 --> 12:40.820
[GIGGLE]

12:40.940 --> 12:42.840
[ED YELLING PLAYFULLY]
C'mon, c'mon!

12:42.840 --> 12:44.520
ED: C'mon, you can't catch me!
NINA: Wait up!

12:44.520 --> 12:45.620
C'mon, slowpokes!

12:47.960 --> 12:49.200
Ha-ha!

12:49.300 --> 12:52.120
I'm gonna get you!
Look out! Here I come!

12:52.300 --> 12:54.300
[AL AND NINA GIGGLING]

12:54.300 --> 12:55.820
ED: [MUFFLED GRUNT]
AL: Huh?

12:55.940 --> 12:58.180
[GIGGLING]

13:00.360 --> 13:04.560
[SOUNDS OF PLAYING
CONTINUE IN THE DISTANCE]

13:07.680 --> 13:10.360
"Don't forget, Assessment Day
is coming soon."

13:18.880 --> 13:22.920
HUGHES: What I wanna know is why this guy is only
targeting State Alchemists and no one else.

13:23.520 --> 13:27.720
If it's the military he's trying to hurt,
he could go after normal soldiers.

13:28.040 --> 13:31.440
Surely soldiers would be easier
to kill than highly skilled Alchemists...

13:31.480 --> 13:34.300
especially ones that
have been State-certified.

13:35.120 --> 13:37.700
Maybe the certification
is the reason.

13:37.840 --> 13:38.320
Hmm?

13:38.400 --> 13:41.300
State Alchemists are given
high pay and special privilege.

13:41.440 --> 13:44.620
There must be any number of people
who envy them for their positions.

13:44.840 --> 13:49.600
Or perhaps they feel they have not upheld
their creed, "Alchemist be thou for the people."

13:49.760 --> 13:56.740
Alchemists who are supposed to be pillars of science and truth are
turned into the military's walking weapons as soon as they receive certification.

13:57.800 --> 13:59.580
There are plenty of people, I'm sure...

13:59.600 --> 14:03.920
Who have not forgotten the role that
State Alchemists played in the Ishvalan Civil War

14:04.100 --> 14:05.120
[KNOCKING ON DOOR]

14:06.660 --> 14:08.100
I have a report, sir.

14:08.400 --> 14:12.580
A canvas has revealed that yesterday,
at 9.30, or right around that time,

14:12.580 --> 14:18.080
a man with a large scar on his face was sighted in the
Central City train station by multiple station employees.

14:18.100 --> 14:21.160
The station?!
Looks like that bastard got away.

14:23.780 --> 14:27.660
Before I earned my State Alchemist
certification, our life was terrible.

14:28.500 --> 14:30.460
We were so poor in those days.

14:31.550 --> 14:36.120
My wife couldn't stand living that
kind of life, so she left us.

14:38.880 --> 14:41.180
I can't afford to
fail this assessment.

14:41.760 --> 14:44.960
I don't wanna go back to those days again.
I don't even think I could.

14:45.300 --> 14:47.300
Don't worry, Daddy,
it's okay!

14:47.300 --> 14:52.180
If those people do tell you no, me and
Alexander will growl at them until they say yes!

14:52.320 --> 14:54.920
[AL GIGGLING]
You tell 'em, Nina!

14:55.900 --> 14:59.700
Hey, Nina. I've got an idea.
Do you want to play with Daddy tomorrow?

14:59.820 --> 15:01.060
Really?!

15:01.180 --> 15:02.060
Yeah.

15:02.360 --> 15:04.060
Woo-hoo!

15:04.320 --> 15:08.180
Alexander! Daddy says he's
going to play with us tomorrow!

15:08.260 --> 15:10.520
[ALEXANDER BARKS]
[ED AND AL CHUCKLING]

15:12.000 --> 15:14.300
[DOORBELL RINGING]

15:19.460 --> 15:23.300
Hello, Mr. Tucker!
Thanks for having us again today!

15:23.940 --> 15:24.860
Huh?

15:26.860 --> 15:28.300
Mr. Tucker?

15:28.320 --> 15:30.300
Hey! Nina?!

15:31.300 --> 15:32.140
[DOOR OPENS]

15:33.120 --> 15:34.300
AL: Mr. Tucker!

15:34.320 --> 15:36.300
ED: There you are!
So you are home.

15:37.300 --> 15:38.300
Yes.

15:38.900 --> 15:41.980
I did it, boys.
I finally did it.

15:42.900 --> 15:45.600
A Chimera that
understands human speech.

15:48.390 --> 15:49.480
Here, let me show you.

15:49.980 --> 15:53.700
Listen to me.
That person over there, that's Edward.

15:53.720 --> 15:56.700
That person... Edward...

15:56.720 --> 15:59.100
Yes, that's very good. Well done!

15:59.160 --> 16:01.780
That's amazing!
It can actually talk!

16:01.800 --> 16:06.060
Now I don't have to worry
about losing my certification!

16:06.660 --> 16:09.500
That person Ed...ward...

16:09.900 --> 16:11.120
Woah...

16:12.220 --> 16:17.760
That person Ed...ward...
That person Ed...ward...

16:18.460 --> 16:20.420
Big brother, Ed...

16:20.420 --> 16:21.920
[GASP]

16:29.900 --> 16:33.920
ED: Mr. Tucker, when did you
first get your state certification?

16:34.020 --> 16:37.200
Let's see...
It was two years ago.

16:38.900 --> 16:41.280
And when did your wife leave you?

16:42.160 --> 16:43.940
That was two years ago, too.

16:44.520 --> 16:47.300
I just have one more
question for you.

16:47.350 --> 16:50.700
Nina and Alexander... Where are they?!

16:50.720 --> 16:51.500
[GASP]

16:55.160 --> 16:57.300
Damn brat, figuring it out so quickly.

16:59.160 --> 17:00.060
Brother!

17:00.260 --> 17:03.520
Oh yeah, I figured it out!
You did it again!

17:03.940 --> 17:06.300
Two years ago, it was your wife,

17:06.300 --> 17:11.040
This time, you used your own daughter
and her dog to transmute a talking Chimera!

17:11.180 --> 17:14.100
You can only do so much
with animals, after all.

17:14.300 --> 17:17.680
It's much easier when you start
with a human, isn't that right?

17:18.440 --> 17:22.380
I don't see what you're so upset about.
This is how we progress.

17:22.420 --> 17:25.660
Human experimentation
is a necessary step.

17:25.700 --> 17:28.420
I would think a scientist
should understand—

17:28.460 --> 17:31.800
ED: Shut up! Do you really think
you can get away with this?!

17:31.980 --> 17:35.990
Messing around with someone's
life like that... Your own daughter!

17:36.080 --> 17:37.660
Someone's life, you say?

17:37.820 --> 17:40.660
[LAUGHS] You'd know all about that,
wouldn't you?

17:40.820 --> 17:43.900
Look at you, Fullmetal Alchemist,
look at your legs...

17:43.960 --> 17:44.940
Your arm...

17:44.940 --> 17:46.120
Your brother...

17:46.280 --> 17:51.000
Those things are also the result of messing
around with somebody's life, aren't they?

17:51.000 --> 17:52.100
Shut up!

17:54.920 --> 17:59.230
[CACKLES] We are the same!
We're the same! You're just like me!

17:59.440 --> 18:00.260
We're not!

18:00.260 --> 18:04.540
Oh, but yes we are! The opportunity
was right in front of us and we took it!

18:04.640 --> 18:07.560
We had to, even though we
knew it was against the rules!

18:07.640 --> 18:08.500
No!

18:09.700 --> 18:10.860
Not me!

18:11.200 --> 18:12.700
Alchemists don't...

18:13.580 --> 18:15.180
Do that!

18:15.720 --> 18:18.720
I'm not... I'm not!

18:18.720 --> 18:20.360
Brother!

18:20.360 --> 18:22.800
If you keep this up,
he'll die!

18:33.700 --> 18:35.580
Edward, no...

18:36.920 --> 18:41.600
Daddy...
Do you... hurt... Daddy?

18:48.000 --> 18:54.380
I'm sorry. Even with all our power,
we can't do anything to change you back.

18:54.780 --> 18:56.240
I'm sorry....

18:56.820 --> 18:58.120
I'm sorry.

18:58.480 --> 19:02.140
Can we play...now?
Can we play now?

19:03.160 --> 19:04.880
I made it just in time.

19:05.020 --> 19:08.140
I get to remain a
State Alchemist...I passed!

19:16.340 --> 19:19.080
[PATHETIC WHIMPERING]

19:20.080 --> 19:24.300
Like hell you're staying a State Alchemist...
Like hell.

19:25.920 --> 19:27.940
Can we... play now?

19:30.740 --> 19:33.960
[PAINED YELLING]
Damn it!

19:37.340 --> 19:40.580
HAWKEYE: If there was an example
of the devil's work in this world...

19:40.760 --> 19:43.020
this world, this case would
definitely be it.

19:43.540 --> 19:45.120
MUSTANG: The devil, huh?

19:45.550 --> 19:48.120
A State Alchemist must
be willing to act,

19:48.240 --> 19:51.920
Able to take another's life
when ordered to, without questioning.

19:52.280 --> 19:57.200
In some ways, Mr. Tucker's actions
and our own may not be all that far apart.

19:57.560 --> 20:00.480
When it comes to interfering
with other people's lives...

20:00.820 --> 20:03.980
We choose our own path,
knowing full well what we're doing.

20:06.380 --> 20:09.720
That's the way it is.
Right, Fullmetal?

20:14.280 --> 20:18.240
You will more than likely come
across cases like this again in the future.

20:18.520 --> 20:21.860
And you may end up having to
get your own hands dirty, as well.

20:22.720 --> 20:25.000
You gonna shut down
like this every time?

20:25.200 --> 20:27.630
We may be called dogs
of the military...

20:27.760 --> 20:29.860
We may even be
cursed as devils.

20:30.040 --> 20:31.200
It doesn't matter.

20:31.280 --> 20:34.180
Al and I are still going to
get our bodies back.

20:34.580 --> 20:36.600
We know the truth.

20:36.780 --> 20:40.880
We know we're not devils.
We know we're not gods.

20:41.920 --> 20:43.120
We're human.

20:45.280 --> 20:48.300
We're only human!

20:50.620 --> 20:54.070
We can't even do anything
to save one innocent little girl.

20:55.840 --> 20:57.840
So what good are we, then?

21:00.160 --> 21:03.160
I wonder why no one's
capable of understanding me.

21:04.280 --> 21:05.340
Nina...

21:09.220 --> 21:11.840
[THUNDER CRACKS]

21:11.860 --> 21:13.760
You're Shou Tucker, correct?

21:13.960 --> 21:18.620
Who are you? Not military.
Who are you?!

21:18.920 --> 21:22.380
How did you get in here?
There were military police out front!

21:23.360 --> 21:26.820
Foolish alchemists who turn
their backs on the ways of God...

21:28.940 --> 21:30.500
...shall be punished.

21:39.120 --> 21:40.900
Daddy's hurting...

21:42.940 --> 21:46.880
Daddy hurts...
No, daddy...

21:47.840 --> 21:49.360
You poor creature.

21:49.440 --> 21:53.380
Once you have been given this form,
there is no way of separating you again.

21:54.350 --> 21:59.940
At least your passing will be in peace.
[THUNDER CRACKS]

22:04.220 --> 22:05.000
God,

22:06.660 --> 22:07.680
Hear me.

22:08.060 --> 22:10.960
Two human souls have
just been returned to you.

22:11.540 --> 22:13.990
Please accept them
into your loving arms.

22:14.220 --> 22:18.620
Please grant these poor lost souls
everlasting peace and salvation.

22:19.800 --> 22:22.300
[THUNDER RUMBLING]

22:28.580 --> 22:34.400
Ano hi mita sora akaneiro no sora o

22:34.480 --> 22:39.700
nee kimi wa oboete imasu ka

22:39.760 --> 22:45.460
Yakusoku chigiri shoka
no kaze ga tsutsumu

22:45.720 --> 22:50.600
futari yorisotta

22:53.680 --> 22:58.860
Muri na egao no ura

22:58.860 --> 23:04.240
nobita kage o kakumau

23:04.280 --> 23:13.620
Dakara kizukanu furi saisei o erabu

23:15.700 --> 23:22.840
Table no ue no furuenai shirase machitsuzukete

23:26.260 --> 23:31.680
kuuhaku no yoru o kuru hazu no nai asa mo

23:31.680 --> 23:35.980
zenbu wakatte'tan da

23:36.060 --> 23:41.540
Ano hi mita sora akaneiro no sora o

23:41.540 --> 23:46.740
nee itsuka omoidasu deshou

23:46.740 --> 23:52.180
Hatasenakatta yakusoku o idaite

23:52.420 --> 23:57.240
futari arukidasu

23:59.200 --> 24:03.400
The rain pours down in East City.

24:03.400 --> 24:09.520
Still grief-stricken over the death of Nina,
Ed and Al are attacked by the mysterious man, Scar.

24:10.020 --> 24:15.740
In a moment of crisis, Ed must make a desperate decision
while the life of his brother hangs in the balance.

24:15.860 --> 24:18.920
Next time on
Fullmetal Alchemist: Brotherhood

24:19.020 --> 24:21.960
Episode 5, Rain of Sorrows

24:23.020 --> 24:25.100
What will Edward decide?

24:25.280 --> 24:28.400
And will he be able to
live with the consequences?
